   "pron": "am-PLYAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You can extend a timetable or a house. Its future is regular: «ampliará».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "biblioteca",
   "significado": "library",
   "pron": "bi-blyo-TE-ka",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is not «librería»: a librería sells books and a biblioteca lends them.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "barrio",
   "significado": "neighbourhood",
   "pron": "BA-rryo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "The «rr» rolls strongly: «BA-rryo». It is the area where your neighbours live.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "préstamo",
   "significado": "loan",
   "pron": "PRES-ta-mo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It has an accent on the e: «PRES-ta-mo». A book loan: you take it and give it back.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "vecinos",
   "significado": "neighbours",
   "pron": "be-THI-nos",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "They live in your building or neighbourhood. Singular: «vecino»; feminine: «vecina».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "horario",
   "significado": "opening hours, timetable",
   "pron": "o-RA-ryo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "A library has a horario: it opens at some hours and closes at others.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "noticia",
   "significado": "news item",
   "pron": "no-TI-thya",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "f",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "A noticia tells something that has happened. The plural is «noticias».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "entre semana",
   "significado": "during the week",
   "pron": "EN-tre se-MA-na",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You say «entre semana», without an article. It is the opposite of the weekend.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "titular",
   "significado": "headline",
   "pron": "ti-tu-LAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "As a noun it is «el titular». It goes above the news item and gives the main idea.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "a partir de",
   "significado": "from … onwards",
   "pron": "a par-TIR de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It marks the start of a change: «a partir del lunes». «De + el» joins as «del».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "cerrar",
   "significado": "to close",
   "pron": "the-RRAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It changes e to ie: «cierro», «cierra». Its opposite is «abrir».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "más tarde",
   "significado": "later",
   "pron": "mas TAR-de",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Dos horas más tarde» compares two times. The opposite is «más temprano».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "amplía",
   "significado": "extends (ampliar)",
   "pron": "am-PLI-a",
