    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Who, what, when and where",
     "texto": [
      "In a short news item, the first sentence and the time and place expressions tell you **what happens**, **when** and **where**.\n\nThen check the details: **who** is affected, **when** a change begins and whether the text gives a **reason**.\n\nNews talks about things that will happen using the **future**: **ampliará**, **cerrará**, **abrirá**. It also uses **a partir de** (from when) and **más tarde que** (comparing times).\n\nThe news item in this lesson is invented and is used for language practice."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "The regular future in news",
     "texto": [
      "The future of regular verbs adds the endings to the **whole infinitive**:\n\n- **-é**, **-ás**, **-á**, **-emos**, **-éis**, **-án**.\n- **ampliar** → **ampliará**; **cerrar** → **cerrará**; **abrir** → **abrirá**.\n\nWith **él / ella / ellos** news uses **-á** and **-án**: **abrirá** (one), **abrirán** (several).\n\n**A partir de** + day marks the start: **a partir del lunes**."
     ],
